NAME
       mkinitcpio - point the boot configuration at the root file system by UUID

SYNOPSIS
       **mkinitcpio** [**-r** __ROOT__] [**-b** __BOOTDIR__] [**-u**] [**-n**]

DESCRIPTION
       The kernel mounts its root file system only when the boot loader gives
       it **root=UUID=**__uuid__ on the kernel command line. **mkinitcpio** finds
       the UUID of the root partition and writes it into every boot entry of
       the Limine configuration on the boot (EFI) partition:

           __BOOTDIR__/limine.conf
           __BOOTDIR__/EFI/BOOT/limine.conf
           __BOOTDIR__/boot/limine/limine.conf

       An entry without a **cmdline:** line gets one; an existing line keeps
       its other options and only its **root=UUID=** part is replaced. Run it
       again whenever the root partition is formatted or moved to another disk.

OPTIONS
       **-r** __ROOT__
              root partition, for example **sda2** or **/dev/sdb2**. Without it
              the partition the system is running from is used.
       **-b** __BOOTDIR__
              where the boot partition is mounted (default **/boot**).
       **-u**   give the root file system a new UUID when it has none (an
              ext2 file system made before UUIDs existed). Without this
              option such a partition is reported and left alone.
       **-n**   do not write anything, print the new configuration.

EXIT STATUS
       0 on success, 1 on error.

SEE ALSO
       blkid(8), mkfs(8), fdisk(8)
